[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SForge Language Specification Track

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-001
TITLE: Source compatibility is an explicit import mode
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge shall treat legacy SPICE source as an explicitly selected import dialect and shall report unsupported, ambiguous or lossy translations structurally.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: legacy library maintainer. Compatibility is a boundary feature, not the canonical grammar.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-002
TITLE: Circuits are unit-checked declarations
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge circuit declarations shall have lexical names, typed terminals and dimension-checked quantities; implicit unit suffix interpretation and silent global parameter capture are prohibited.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: analog designer. The grammar must preserve familiar devices while making physical meaning explicit.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-003
TITLE: Runs express verification intent
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge run declarations shall model analysis, observable selection, assertions, sweeps, random seed and failure policy as typed syntax mapped into the shared simulation IR.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: verification engineer. A source file must replay a result without hidden console or GUI state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-004
TITLE: Device extensions are bounded capabilities
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge device extensions shall declare terminals, parameters, units, state, supported analyses, derivatives and deterministic capability requirements before any native or GPU implementation is selected.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: compact-model author. Native code is acceleration, not language semantics.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-005
TITLE: Parser implementation preserves diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
The first SForge parser shall preserve UTF-8 source spans, recover at declaration boundaries, emit multiple structured diagnostics where safe, and lower only syntactically valid declarations into a parser-independent AST.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: IDE and automation engineer. Parlot is the initial parser candidate; the AST/diagnostic contract must keep the parser replaceable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-006
TITLE: Results are portable typed data
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge shall map observed values and run provenance to stable typed result schemas independently of the chosen ngspice, Rust, CPU or GPU backend.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Design review lens: automation/API engineer. Arrow and Parquet are delivery formats, not simulator-specific text scraping.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-007
TITLE: Lexical safety and fuzz resilience
STATEMENT: >>>
The SForge lexer shall report token source locations, reject malformed numeric prefixes and unexpected characters deterministically, and be exercised with seeded malformed-input fuzz cases that must not throw.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/SForge.Language/Lexer.cs. Verification: SForge.Language.Conformance deterministic seed 0x5F0A6E, 2000 generated malformed cases.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-008
TITLE: Validated v0.1 lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
The validated v0.1 SForge AST shall lower primitive circuit declarations and transient runs into the existing typed simulator request contract, including the SForge gnd to simulator 0 mapping.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/SForge.Language/Lowering.cs. Verification: SForge.Language.Conformance lowers and executes examples/clamp.sforge through the Rust executable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SFL-009
TITLE: Observable and assertion lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
SForge v0.1 shall lower v(node) and i(device) observations to typed result measurements, and shall lower the supported max(signal) < quantity requirement form to a bounded native measurement/assertion pair.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/SForge.Language/Lowering.cs. Verification: SForge.Language.Conformance verifies the lowered experiment and successful Rust execution.
<<<
